---
import System from "../components/landing/System.astro";
import "../components/landing/Landing.css";
import "../styles/site/tokens.css";
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <meta
      name="description"
      content="Effect-native durable jobs. Schema-defined work, atomic PostgreSQL enqueue, and explicit scoped workers."
    />
    <meta name="theme-color" content="#090b10" />
    <title>effect-jobs — Give background work a durable home</title>
  </head>
  <body class="ej-landing">
    <a class="skip" href="#main">Skip to content</a>
    <header class="site-header wrap">
      <a class="wordmark" href="/" aria-label="effect-jobs home"
        ><span class="mark" aria-hidden="true">e<span>j</span></span
        >effect-jobs</a
      >
      <nav aria-label="Main navigation">
        <a href="/docs">Documentation</a><a href="/demo"
          >Demo <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a
        >
      </nav>
      <span class="alpha">PUBLIC ALPHA</span>
    </header>
    <main id="main">
      <section class="hero wrap" aria-labelledby="promise">
        <div class="eyebrow">
          <span class="tiny-mark" aria-hidden="true"></span> DURABLE EXECUTION ·
          NATIVE EFFECT
        </div>
        <h1 id="promise">
          Your request ends.<br /><span>The work goes on.</span>
        </h1>
        <p class="hero-copy">
          Give background work a durable home. Schema-defined jobs, atomic
          PostgreSQL enqueue, and scoped workers that compose with your Effect
          application.
        </p>
        <div class="actions">
          <a class="primary" href="/docs/start/first-job"
            >Build your first job <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a
          ><a class="secondary" href="/demo"
            >Explore the demo <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a
          >
        </div>
        <p class="hero-note">
          Your database. Your transactions. Explicit execution.
        </p>
        <System />
      </section>
      <section class="stack-strip wrap" aria-label="Supported stack">
        <span>BUILT TO COMPOSE</span><strong>Effect 4.0.5</strong><i
          aria-hidden="true">/</i
        ><strong>PostgreSQL</strong><i aria-hidden="true">/</i><strong
          >Node.js · Bun</strong
        ><i aria-hidden="true">/</i><strong>Optional Drizzle</strong>
      </section>
      <section class="atomic wrap section" aria-labelledby="atomic-title">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">01 / CLOSE THE GAP</p><h2 id="atomic-title">
            The write and the work.<br /><span>One transaction.</span>
          </h2><p>
            A report request is only useful if its job exists too. Join
            application writes and enqueue in the same configured client
            transaction: commit together, or roll back together.
          </p><a class="text-link" href="/docs/persistence/transactions"
            >Understand atomic enqueue <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a
          >
        </div>
        <div class="transaction-card">
          <div class="panel-label">
            <span>TRANSACTION BOUNDARY</span><span class="status-dot"
              >same client</span
            >
          </div><ol>
            <li>
              <span>01</span><div>
                <strong>Save report request</strong><small
                  >Application-owned business data</small
                >
              </div>
            </li><li>
              <span>02</span><div>
                <strong>Enqueue report job</strong><small
                  >Producer identity + encoded payload</small
                >
              </div>
            </li><li>
              <span>03</span><div>
                <strong>Commit together</strong><small
                  >Joined enqueue results are provisional until commit</small
                >
              </div>
            </li>
          </ol><div class="identity">
            <span>REPEATED REQUEST?</span><p>
              The same <code>(operation, operationId, slot)</code> and matching semantics
              find the retained job. Changed semantics produce a conflict.
            </p><a href="/docs/persistence/deduplication"
              >How deduplication works →</a
            >
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>
      <section
        class="wrap section reliability"
        aria-labelledby="reliability-title"
      >
        <p class="eyebrow">02 / MAKE FAILURE EXPLICIT</p><div
          class="section-heading"
        >
          <h2 id="reliability-title">
            Reliability has<br /><span>more than one path.</span>
          </h2><p>
            Retries are a policy. Ownership is a lease. An uncertain external
            outcome still needs application-level reconciliation.
          </p>
        </div><div class="principles">
          <article>
            <span class="principle-icon" aria-hidden="true">↻</span><h3>
              Retries that persist
            </h3><p>
              A confirmed retry stores the next availability using the first
              persisted policy and a bounded attempt budget.
            </p><a href="/docs/execution/retries">Retry semantics →</a>
          </article><article>
            <span class="principle-icon" aria-hidden="true">⌁</span><h3>
              Ownership that fences
            </h3><p>
              Database-time leases and exact ownership checks guard durable
              finalization. External side effects still need idempotency.
            </p><a href="/docs/execution/recovery">Leases & recovery →</a>
          </article><article>
            <span class="principle-icon" aria-hidden="true">?</span><h3>
              Unknown stays unknown
            </h3><p>
              A lost response does not prove rollback. OutcomeUnknown is an
              attempt outcome, not a durable job state or permission to replay.
            </p><a href="/docs/concepts/lifecycle">Follow the lifecycle →</a>
          </article>
        </div>
      </section>
      <section class="wrap section finish">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">SMALL CORE. EXPLICIT BOUNDARIES.</p><h2>
            Make the next request<br /><span
              >the start of something durable.</span
            >
          </h2><p>
            Current alpha: PostgreSQL persistence, application-owned migrations
            and pools, explicit worker lifetime. Read the supported setup before
            integrating.
          </p>
        </div><a class="primary" href="/docs/start/installation"
          >Read the installation guide <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a
        >
      </section>
    </main>
    <footer class="wrap">
      <a class="wordmark" href="/">effect-jobs</a><p>
        Durable jobs, composed with Effect.
      </p><a href="/docs">Documentation →</a>
    </footer>
  </body>
</html>
